in the Software under these terms. Each Licensor grants only rights that it
owns or is entitled to license. Exercising rights granted by this license
constitutes acceptance of its conditions.

An "Official PEX Deployment" is a PEX/PDex protocol deployment identified as
official by the maintainers of https://github.com/ultrade-org/pex-ts-pubsdk,
including its official upgrades and official test networks. Merely copying
its code, parameters, names, or metadata does not make a deployment official.

2. Commercial builder permission

Subject to this license, the Licensors grant you a worldwide, non-exclusive,
royalty-free copyright license to use, reproduce, modify, prepare derivative
works of, and distribute the Software in source or compiled form to develop,
operate, maintain, and support products that integrate with Official PEX
Deployments.

Permitted products include independently branded trading interfaces, wallets,
bots, liquidity tools, analytics, SDK adaptations, and backend services. You
may charge for your products and services, collect protocol-supported builder
fees, serve your own customers, and run your own nodes, indexers, databases,
and compatible HTTP APIs. You are not required to use a PEX-operated backend.
These uses are permitted even if your interface or service competes with a
PEX-operated interface or service on the same Official PEX Deployments.

You may include the Software in a product that also supports other protocols,
provided the Software and derivatives of it are used only for its PEX
integration and not to implement, operate, or support those other protocols.

You may also use and modify the Software for education, evaluation, security
research, and non-production testing, including isolated local deployments.
This testing permission does not authorize operating an independent protocol
for public trading or accepting real customer funds on such a deployment.

3. Independent protocol restriction

You may not use, modify, distribute, or provide the Software or derivatives
of it to create, launch, operate, commercialize, or materially support a
separate exchange, trading, liquidity, or lending protocol that is a substitute
for or competes with PEX/PDex outside Official PEX Deployments. This includes
forks or copies of PEX contracts and independent deployments using different
contract addresses, names, operators, interfaces, or networks. It applies to
both free and paid offerings and to providing the Software to others for
those purposes. The non-production uses expressly permitted in section 2
remain permitted.

This is a condition on use of the Software, not a restriction on independently
written software that does not contain, derive from, or use the Software.
Uses outside this license require separate written permission from the
relevant Licensors.

